{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 A-Lift\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Four-band "encode-only" lift, in the spirit of running a source through an A-type noise-reduction encoder without decoding it. Each band gets about +10 dB well below Threshold (about +14 dB at the very top), fading as the signal gets louder.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Custom GUI with a per-band lift meter. Knobs: drag (Shift = fine), mouse wheel, double-click to reset; click a value to type it. LINK THR trims Output while you turn Threshold so the level stays roughly constant.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires the tk-gui-tools library (tk_gui_tools.jsfx-inc). With ReaPack, install the "tk-gui-tools" package from this repository as well.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 P-Clip\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Soft clipper modelled on the Soft Clip Pro mode of SIR Audio Tools' StandardCLIP. Saturation goes from a plain hard clip (0 %) to a soft knee that squeezes the last 24 dB below the clip level into 12 dB and adds 12 dB of gain (100 %). Clip Level sets where the clip sits, from 0 down to -24 dBFS, and Input Gain drives the signal into it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Only the input gain, the clip level and that clip curve are modelled: no output gain, ceiling or oversampling. Not affiliated with SIR Audio Tools.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Custom GUI with the transfer curve, a dot showing where the input sits on it, and a gain-reduction meter with peak hold and a resettable maximum (click the meter). Knobs: drag (Shift = fine), mouse wheel, double-click to reset; click a value to type it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Requires the tk-gui-tools library (tk_gui_tools.jsfx-inc). With ReaPack, install the "tk-gui-tools" package from this repository as well.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 tk-gui-tools\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The JSFX library that draws the GUIs of the effects in this repository (A-Lift, P-Clip). Install it once, next to the effects; it is shared by all of them.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This package installs only tk_gui_tools.jsfx-inc. The library is written by John Matthews (Tukan Studios) and is redistributed here with his permission; its terms are at the top of that file. The full archive, with examples and documentation, is at https://stash.reaper.fm/v/53055/tk-gui-tools.zip\par}
}
